# Correction Q1: No, the prior motion is too subtle and lacks the assertive quality of a stop command; the small forward push is barely perceptible and looks more like a static hold.
# Correction Q2: The entire sequence should be changed to show the arm moving from a neutral, lower position into the high, extended stop pose. This should be a single, sharp motion, followed by a firm hold, to create a clear and authoritative gesture.
# Q1: How would a human perform this motion? A human would raise their hand from a neutral position, palm facing forward, and extend it firmly towards the person they are signaling to stop.
# Q2: Pose Candidates Comparison. Rank at least 2 pose configurations (torso_height, arm_position, gripper_orientation, head, left_arm, x/y/z) and state the winner and why—do NOT pick presets from gesture names alone. Candidate 1: Start in the final extended pose and do a small push forward (the prior attempt). Candidate 2: Start with the arm lower and closer to the body, then move into the final extended pose. Winner is Candidate 2 because the movement into the pose is the most communicative part of the gesture.
# Q3: Structure Comparison. Compare 2+ full primitive sequences (e.g., M1: pose > movement > pose vs M2: pose > path > path). State the winner and why—**prioritize movement/path beats that express the cue**, not pose-only tweaks. M1: pose (start low) -> path (move up) -> path (move forward). M2: pose (start low) -> pose (end high/extended). Winner is M2; a `pose` to `pose` transition creates a single, decisive, and smooth motion into the final stop configuration, which feels more natural and assertive than two separate path steps.
# Q4: Context Reinforcement. Compare 2+ micro-timing choices (speed, repetition, hold_time, torso/head expression) that make the gesture read stronger and pick the best one. Option 1: A slow, deliberate movement into the pose. Option 2: A fast, sharp movement into the pose, followed by a long hold. Winner is Option 2; the speed conveys urgency, and the long hold reinforces the command to stop and hold position.
